      "anchor_id": "issue-gothrumedia-gothru-360-viewer-10",
      "display_title": "Issue #10: Fix Issue Google Drive Connection Doesn't Work",
      "main_description_html": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Feedback</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>albug</strong> — 7:55 PM<br>\nOne thing that doesn't work is the Google drive connection<br>\nOn both apps</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Google Drive backup (sign-in / connect) fails for the tester on <strong>both apps</strong>. Since it reproduces on both, the cause is almost certainly server-side OAuth configuration in Google Cloud rather than platform code.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Where it lives</h2>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Piece</th>\n<th>File</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Drive service — sign-in, folder, rsync, resumable upload</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">lib/services/drive_backup.dart</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Riverpod state + backup loop</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">lib/state/backup_providers.dart</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Local mirror of what's on Drive (Hive)</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">lib/data/backup_store.dart</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Backup screen (select-all + per-image)</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">lib/views/backup_screen.dart</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Per-image entry point</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">lib/views/asset_actions.dart</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>iOS OAuth client id + URL scheme</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">ios/Runner/Info.plist</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Setup notes</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\">GCP project: <strong>silicon-topic-858</strong>. Scope: <code class=\"notranslate\">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file</code> (non-sensitive).</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Suspected root causes (ranked)</h2>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">1. OAuth consent screen is still in <strong>Testing</strong> — affects BOTH apps <g-emoji class=\"g-emoji\" alias=\"warning\">⚠️</g-emoji> most likely</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md</code> records the consent screen as <strong>Testing</strong>, which means:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Only email addresses explicitly added as <strong>test users</strong> can sign in at all. Anyone else gets blocked (\"app has not completed verification\" / <code class=\"notranslate\">access_denied</code>) — this alone would make Drive fail on both Android and iOS for a tester who isn't on the list.</li>\n<li>Refresh tokens expire after <strong>7 days</strong>, so even allow-listed testers get silently kicked out roughly weekly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The code already has a workaround for the second symptom — <code class=\"notranslate\">DriveBackup._isReauthCanceled</code> retries once on Credential Manager's <code class=\"notranslate\">[16] Account reauth failed</code> — which is a strong hint this is already biting in practice.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Fix:</strong> flip the consent screen to <strong>Production</strong>. Because <code class=\"notranslate\">drive.file</code> is non-sensitive this needs <strong>no Google security assessment</strong> — only the basic branding/support-email fields.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">2. Android OAuth client SHA-1 is stale — affects Android only</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Android OAuth client is registered with only the <strong>debug</strong> keystore SHA-1:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"A9:84:94:7E:83:B8:DC:B0:75:AF:4C:56:10:E4:04:D7:93:84:8A:0F\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">A9:84:94:7E:83:B8:DC:B0:75:AF:4C:56:10:E4:04:D7:93:84:8A:0F\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md</code> justifies that with \"the <code class=\"notranslate\">release</code> build currently signs with the debug config too\" — <strong>that is no longer true.</strong> <code class=\"notranslate\">android/app/build.gradle.kts</code> now signs release with the upload keystore from <code class=\"notranslate\">android/key.properties</code>, and Play App Signing re-signs with a third key on top:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-kotlin notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"signingConfig = if (hasReleaseKeystore) {\n    signingConfigs.getByName(&quot;release&quot;)\n} else {\n    signingConfigs.getByName(&quot;debug&quot;)\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">signingConfig <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> (hasReleaseKeystore) {\n    signingConfigs.getByName(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>release<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n} <span class=\"pl-k\">else</span> {\n    signingConfigs.getByName(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>debug<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Android's Credential Manager authenticates by <em>package name + SHA-1</em>. Any build not signed with the debug key therefore fails with <code class=\"notranslate\">ApiException: 10 (DEVELOPER_ERROR)</code> — which the app surfaces as the generic \"Google sign-in failed. Please try again.\"</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Fix:</strong> add both missing SHA-1s to the Android OAuth client:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>the upload keystore's SHA-1 (<code class=\"notranslate\">keytool -list -v -keystore &lt;upload.jks&gt; -alias &lt;alias&gt;</code>)</li>\n<li>the <strong>Play App Signing</strong> SHA-1 from Play Console → Setup → App integrity</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">3. iOS config — verified consistent, deprioritized</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Checked and matching, so probably not the iOS cause:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = co.360viewer.gothru</code> (note: no \"u\" — deliberately differs from Android's <code class=\"notranslate\">co.u360viewer.gothru</code>)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">GIDClientID</code> = <code class=\"notranslate\">...-ia2vs2csb04sabkku3c5anps8ekkea1u.apps.googleusercontent.com</code></li>\n<li>reversed client id present in <code class=\"notranslate\">CFBundleURLSchemes</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Still worth confirming the iOS OAuth client in GCP is registered against Team ID <code class=\"notranslate\">W433ZFZCX5</code> and that bundle id.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">4. Errors are unreadable — blocks diagnosis either way</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">BackupController._message()</code> collapses every non-cancel/non-interrupt <code class=\"notranslate\">GoogleSignInException</code> into one string:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-dart notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"default:\n  return 'Google sign-in failed. Please try again.';\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">default</span><span class=\"pl-k\">:</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'Google sign-in failed. Please try again.'</span>;</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Google status code (10 / 12500 / 16) and description are dropped, so a tester's report can't distinguish SHA-1 mismatch from an unverified-app block from a network failure. That is why this report arrives as \"doesn't work\" with nothing actionable attached.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Acceptance criteria</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Reproduce and capture the real error on Android (<code class=\"notranslate\">adb logcat</code> / GoogleSignInException code) and on iOS</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Add the upload-keystore SHA-1 <strong>and</strong> the Play App Signing SHA-1 to the Android OAuth client in GCP project <code class=\"notranslate\">silicon-topic-858</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Verify the iOS OAuth client's bundle id + Team ID, and that the Drive API is enabled on the project</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Move the OAuth consent screen from <strong>Testing</strong> to <strong>Production</strong> (no security assessment needed for <code class=\"notranslate\">drive.file</code>)</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Surface the underlying Google error code/description in the snackbar (or at minimum log it) instead of the generic \"Google sign-in failed\"</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> End-to-end verify on a <strong>release</strong> build from Play (not just a debug build): sign in → GoThru folder created → photo + video upload → rsync skips already-uploaded assets on a second run</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Verify the same flow on a TestFlight/release iOS build</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Update <code class=\"notranslate\">GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md</code> — the \"release signs with the debug config\" note is now stale, and record the final publishing status</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Notes</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The Testing-mode 7-day expiry means this bug can <em>appear fixed</em> and silently regress a week later. Confirm the fix after Production is live, not before.</li>\n<li>Uploads consume each user's own 15 GB Drive quota; the Drive API itself is free, so this is not a billing/quota-exhaustion issue on our side.</li>\n</ul>",
